# WN22-DC-000010: Windows Server 2022 must only allow administrators responsible for the domain controller to have Administrator rights on the system.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: high
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000010-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `critical`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must only allow administrators responsible for the domain controller to have Administrator rights on the system.`
    description `An account that does not have Administrator duties must not have Administrator rights. Such rights would allow the account to bypass or modify required security restrictions on that machine and make it vulnerable to attack. System administrators must log on to systems using only accounts with the minimum level of authority necessary. Standard user accounts must not be members of the built-in Administrators group.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,high,local-group,membership,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-6(10)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Configure the Administrators group to include only administrator groups or accounts that are responsible for the system. Remove any standard user accounts.`

    component_id `comp-windows-local-group`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by ensuring local group 'Administrators' does not contain forbidden principals (Domain controller local Administrators group must not contain Guest, Everyone, or anonymous principals.). The ESP scanner queries state via the windows_local_group CTN and fails the policy if the observed value does not match. Remediation: Use net localgroup or Remove-LocalGroupMember to remove forbidden principals.`
    impl_AC_6_10 `Windows Server implements AC-6(10) by ensuring local group 'Administrators' does not contain forbidden principals (Domain controller local Administrators group must not contain Guest, Everyone, or anonymous principals.). The ESP scanner queries state via the windows_local_group CTN and fails the policy if the observed value does not match. Remediation: Use net localgroup or Remove-LocalGroupMember to remove forbidden principals.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        name `Administrators`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE exists_check
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END
    STATE forbid_member_1
        members string not_contains `Guest`
    STATE_END
    STATE forbid_member_2
        members string not_contains `Everyone`
    STATE_END
    STATE forbid_member_3
        members string not_contains `ANONYMOUS`
    STATE_END
    STATE forbid_member_4
        members string not_contains `NT AUTHORITY\ANONYMOUS LOGON`
    STATE_END
    STATE forbid_member_5
        members string not_contains `NULL SID`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_local_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF exists_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_local_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_member_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_local_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_member_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_local_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_member_3
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_local_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_member_4
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_local_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_member_5
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
